WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.035
-My first guest tonight is an
Emmy-nominated actor.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:08.240
He stars in "This is Us", which
airs Tuesdays at 9 PM on NBC.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.277
Everyone, please welcome
Milo Ventimiglia!

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.879
Come on! [ Laughs ]

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.947
Look at you, man!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:16.449
See.
-What's up, man?

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.550
-Come on, buddy.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.818
I appreciate you coming back to
the show.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.119
Last time you were on the show,

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.622
I don't know if you remember
this, I actually gave you

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.424
my wife's phone number by
mistake.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:27.260
-How can I forget?
How can I forget

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.728
when anybody gives me their
wife's phone number?

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.996
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.130
We were talking and

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.365
I wanted to see if you had
a picture of you.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.502
-I was Evel Knievel.
-So I love Evel Knievel,

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.069
and it was you dressed up --

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:38.505
it was a screen test for
Evel Knievel,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.273
and you're like, "I'll send it
to you, but don't show it."

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.574
And I go, "Yeah,
because it's us."

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.409
I go, "Great," and I couldn't
remember my number,

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.545
so I go, and I just rattled off
my number,

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.014
which I thought was mine,
but it was my wife's.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.582
And it halfway through --
-And so,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:53.552
I sent -- yeah, so I send the
photo of me, full dressed --

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:56.489
this is like, my camera test of
Evel Knievel.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.092
Not test -- like, we were
two days away from filing.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:02.228
I was blonde, I was
hairy-chested, I was everything.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:07.934
And yeah, I didn't put anything.
I just sent the photo.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.968
Yeah.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.103
-And then I got the,
"Who is this?"

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.873
-[ Laughs ] I'm sorry.
Oh, yeah.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.307
My wife was laughing about it
afterwards,

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.777
I was like, "I'm sorry, I just
gave Milo Ventimiglia

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.946
your phone number."
That's so weird.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.782
But anyways, we're big fans at
the house, so...

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.285
-Yeah. Yeah. I'm sure
it went over great.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.453
-Is this your office?
Or is this --

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:30.189
Where --
-Yeah, this is my office

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.790
at home in Los Angeles.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.461
I'm just, you know...
Got some artwork on the walls,

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.996
some Michael Muller, some stuff.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.431
Just kinda hanging out.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.732
There's things on, like,
every wall.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.867
-I'm looking at one sign that
I can see

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.270
in the upper left-hand corner,
because you know I'm a fan

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.573
of yours since "Gilmore Girls",
and it says...

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.708
-Oh, yeah. Yeah, right here.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.110
-"I love..."

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.845
"I love Dean?"
-It says, uh...

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.681
-[ Laughs ]
-"I love Dean 4 Ever."

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:55.848
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:58.184
-And that was the certificate
that you get

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.618
when you're nominated for
an Emmy.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:03.088
-Oh, my gosh! Is that rubbing it
in his face?

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:04.790
What is that?
[ Laughs ]

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.259
-No, no. Not at all.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.562
I mean, you know, Jared and I
are really good friends

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:14.099
and I made the sign for some
photograph that was --

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:16.335
somebody was looking for online
or something,

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:19.972
and so I made the sign,
and after I made it,

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:21.741
I just said, "Well, let me just
hang onto this,

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.377
because this is cool, and I
literally just kind of stuck it

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.346
right onto my Emmy notification
that was, you know --

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:28.647
hanging on my wall.
-It just happened to be there.

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:30.616
Yeah, just, no big deal.
It just happened to be there.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:31.550
-Yeah, no big deal.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:32.752
-Yeah, no big deal.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.487
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.956
-But I want to talk about
"This Is Us."

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:40.225
But I also want to thank you for
doing the stuff you do

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:42.929
for Red Nose Day
on NBC's --

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.363
-Yeah.
-It's a big deal,

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.899
and man, you've been with them
for a couple years now,

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.301
doing some good work.

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:52.004
-Yeah, I mean, you know, I've
been in the NBC family

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.840
for a very long time, and NBC
has always supported

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.777
Red Nose Day, so, you know,
in 2019 --

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:02.314
It's wild, I keep thinking 2019
was last year, but it wasn't.

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:03.649
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:08.120
-But in 2019, I got a chance to
actually go and see

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.790
how the donations were
benefiting these kids

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.892
in pretty impoverished places.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.328
And, yeah, we were in Kenya,

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:18.765
and seeing kids getting
inoculated

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:22.101
for, like, the very, very simple
sickness and disease

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.904
that kids shouldn't have to
deal with, but, you know,

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.039
they're in bad situations.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:33.145
I really was able to see
first-hand what the organization

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:35.214
was doing to better the lives of
these kids.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.282
-Well, thank you for doing that.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.784
-I'm still involved with them.
Yeah.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:40.152
-I want to talk about
"This Is Us."

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:41.554
You never tell me what's going
to happen,

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.889
which is, I understand, but
my question for you

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:47.326
is, do you know
what you're doing?

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:48.895
-This year?
-Yeah.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.329
-Yeah, do I know what I'm doing.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.198
-No, I mean, you definitely know
what you're doing.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.466
But...
-Usually,

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:58.437
Dan Fogelman, he'll come to set
-- and this is the difference

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:03.576
between, let's say, COVID set
versus normal filming set.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.879
In a COVID set, Fogelman
doesn't visit,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.382
so we don't get that sitting
around the campfire,

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:12.151
Dan, having just walked out of
the writer's room,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.920
saying, "You guys want to know
what happens in the next

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.923
7 or 8 or 9 episodes?"

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:20.459
So, we don't really have that
this year,

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.261
so I'm kind of, like,
in the dark.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:25.231
-I know that next season is
supposed to be

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:28.067
the final season.
The series finale.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.102
-That's what we're hearing,
yeah.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:34.039
-Yeah. So, do you know anything
about that?

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.808
Or is this the way --
-Oh yeah, totally.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.344
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.045
-Yeah, of course you do.

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:43.449
I do want to show a clip --
here's Milo Ventimiglia

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.252
in tomorrow night's episode of
"This Is Us."

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.319
Take a look.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:51.390
♪♪

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.558
-Hey, man.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.559
-Hey.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:54.961
-Hey, so I got
the hot chocolate.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.562
-Uh-huh.
-I got the corn syrup

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.799
for the candy apples,
and I bought every box

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.101
of string lights they had at the
hardware store.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.569
-What a guy.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.204
-Hey, do me a favor
and look at this.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.507
I mean, did I get these letters
even?

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.108
-Yeah.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.210
You spelled "carnival" wrong.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.078
[ Laughs ] I'm kidding.
No.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:14.279
It looks great, man.

00:05:14.279 --> 00:05:16.148
-Great's not good enough,
Miguel.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:17.683
I need this proposal
to be perfect.

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:20.352
-Jack, you are recreating
your first date with Rebecca

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.255
in her apartment.
It's exactly the kind of

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.323
romantic gesture that makes
other guys hate you.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:25.591
-Come on, other guys
don't hate me.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.726
-Yeah, they do.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.427
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:29.762
-Yeah, they do.
-No, they don't.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.996
We love you.

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.965
Hey, you got to give my best to
Mandy as well,

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:36.268
because I know she's a new mom
and that's so cool

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:37.670
We love her.
-It's exciting.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.573
She actually -- baby Gus was set
the other day, last week --

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.207
it was exciting.
It was exciting to see her

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:44.877
as a mom. I mean, we've been
playing parents for so long,

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.779
but, like -- yeah, she's a mom.
She's a real mom.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.013
-[ Laughs ] That's fantastic.

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.882
Give her my best.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.084
Milo Ventimiglia, everybody!

